// Title: Unusual File Deletion by Dns.exe
// Sigma ID: 8f0b1fb1-9bd4-4e74-8cdf-a8de4d2adfd0
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Tim Rauch (Nextron Systems), Elastic (idea)
// Date: 2022-09-27 | Modified: 2023-02-15
// ATT&CK: persistence, initial-access, T1133
// Description: Detects an unexpected file being deleted by dns.exe which my indicate activity related to remote
//   code execution or other forms of exploitation as seen in CVE-2020-1350 (SigRed)
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/security/current/unusual-file-modification-by-dns-exe.html
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/file/file_delete/file_delete_win_unusual_deletion_by_dns_exe.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where ActionType =~ "FileDeleted" and (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\dns.exe" and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\dns.log")))
